1 0 0 1 64.00 536.49 Tm
(-  An API key for at least one model provider.) Tj
1 0 0 1 64.00 518.26 Tm
(-  Clone the starter repository and run the smoke test - it should print a model response.) Tj
1 0 0 1 64.00 500.04 Tm
(-  Skim Lewis et al. \(2020\). Do not study it; we read it together.) Tj
/F2 14 Tf
1 0 0 1 64.00 458.56 Tm
(After session 1 - Index something you care about) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 64.00 439.33 Tm
(-  Point the indexer at a corpus of your own: your docs, a wiki export, a set of PDFs.) Tj
1 0 0 1 64.00 421.11 Tm
(-  Write ten questions a colleague might genuinely ask of it.) Tj
1 0 0 1 64.00 402.88 Tm
(-  Run them. Bring the three worst answers to session 2, with the retrieved passages.) Tj
/F2 14 Tf
1 0 0 1 64.00 361.40 Tm
(After session 2 - Rebuild the pipeline) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 64.00 342.18 Tm
(-  Swap the chunking strategy and measure the difference rather than guessing at it.) Tj
1 0 0 1 64.00 323.95 Tm
(-  Add sparse retrieval alongside dense; compare on your own ten questions.) Tj
1 0 0 1 64.00 305.73 Tm
(-  Add a reranker. Record the latency cost as well as the quality change.) Tj
/F2 14 Tf
1 0 0 1 64.00 264.25 Tm
(After session 3 - Build the harness) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 64.00 245.02 Tm
(-  Turn your ten questions into a scored test set with known-correct passages.) Tj
1 0 0 1 64.00 226.80 Tm
(-  Add at least three questions the corpus cannot answer.) Tj
1 0 0 1 64.00 208.57 Tm
(-  Get the harness running from one command. You will use it for the rest of the cohort.) Tj
/F2 14 Tf
1 0 0 1 64.00 167.09 Tm
